{"title":"Elastohydrodynamic film","markdown":{"headingText":"Elastohydrodynamic film","headingAttr":{"id":"sec-ehd-film","classes":[],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n`apps/ehd_film` — the highest-order evolution operator in the shipped set:\nsixth order in space.\n\n## Physical setting\n\nA viscous liquid film confined beneath a thin elastic plate. The plate resists\nbending, that bending sets the pressure in the gap, the pressure gradient\ndrives lubrication flow, and the flow changes the gap. This is the\nelastohydrodynamic problem behind compliant bearings, soft contacts, and\nadhesive films — anywhere a thin fluid layer is bounded by something that\ndeforms.\n\n## Governing equations\n\n$$\np \\;=\\; B\\nabla^4 h \\;-\\; \\gamma\\nabla^2 h \\;-\\; \\Pi(h),\n\\qquad\n\\partial_t h \\;=\\; \\nabla\\cdot\\big[M_0\\nabla p\\big].\n$$ {#eq-ehd-pde}\n\nThe chain is worth reading in order: plate curvature $\\to$ bending pressure\n($B\\nabla^4h$) $\\to$ pressure gradient $\\to$ viscous flux $\\to$ $\\partial_t h$.\nThe bending term is already fourth order, and the divergence of the flux adds\ntwo more, so the evolution operator is $\\nabla^6$.\n\n## Spectral formulation\n\nWith $u = k_{\\mathrm{lap}}$,\n\n$$\nL(k) \\;=\\; M_0 B\\,u^3 \\;-\\; M_0\\gamma\\,u^2 \\;-\\; M_0\\Pi'(h_0)\\,u ,\n\\qquad\nM_{\\mathrm{nl}}(k) \\;=\\; -M_0\\,u .\n$$ {#eq-ehd-symbol}\n\nIn terms of $|\\mathbf{k}| = k$,\n\n$$\n\\lambda(k) \\;=\\; -M_0 B k^6 \\;-\\; M_0\\gamma k^4 \\;+\\; M_0\\Pi'(h_0)k^2 .\n$$ {#eq-ehd-growth}\n\nThe defaults $A = \\gamma = 0$ leave pure bending relaxation,\n$\\lambda = -M_0Bk^6$, which is an exact analytical target.\n\n## Why this chapter is the stiffness argument\n\n@eq-ehd-growth is where the case for ETD is easiest to see. An explicit step on\na grid of spacing $\\Delta x$ would require\n\n$$\n\\Delta t \\;\\lesssim\\; \\frac{\\Delta x^6}{M_0 B\\,\\pi^6},\n$$ {#eq-ehd-cfl}\n\na sixth power of the mesh size. Halving $\\Delta x$ costs a factor of 64 in\ntimestep on top of the factor of $2^d$ in cells per step. ETD treats the $k^6$\noperator as a pointwise multiply by $e^{L\\Delta t}$, which is unconditionally\nstable, and the timestep is then set by accuracy and by the nonlinearity\ninstead.\n\nThe implementation difference between this sixth-order model and the\nfourth-order @sec-thin-film is one extra term in @eq-ehd-symbol.\n\n## Solution strategy\n\nETD1 as in @eq-etd1, dealiased.\n\n## Verification\n\n* **Exact $k^6$ decay.** A single mode decays as $e^{-M_0Bk^6t}$.\n* **Two-mode ratio of 64.** Doubling the wave number multiplies the decay rate\n  by $2^6 = 64$; the measured ratio matches.\n* **Mean-gap conservation.** The mean of $h$ is preserved.\n\n## Binaries and inputs\n\n`ehd_film` (CPU), `ehd_film_hip`. Preset `relaxation.json`.\n\n## Scalability\n\nNot measured.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-outp